This one?

703
00:26:37,940 --> 00:26:39,640
474！
Route 474!

704
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,340
キラキラ！
It's shiny!

705
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:41,540
キラキラ〜！
So shiny!

706
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:45,140
長野から静岡！
Nagano to Shizuoka!

707
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:46,040
え？
Huh?

708
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:47,540
これどうなってんですか？
What is going on here?

709
00:26:46,940 --> 00:26:48,640
長野から静岡...
Nagano to Shizuoka...

710
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,740
474のこの...
On 474, this...

711
00:26:49,540 --> 00:26:51,540
なんか途中で切れてるのじゃ！
It's cut off in the middle!

712
00:26:51,640 --> 00:26:52,640
え？
Huh?

713
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:53,440
ん？
Hmm?

714
00:26:53,140 --> 00:26:53,840
え？
What?

715
00:26:53,740 --> 00:26:55,440
長野から静岡...
Nagano to Shizuoka...

716
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:55,640
え？
Eh?

717
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:56,340
あ、やっぱ...
Ah, wait...

718
00:26:56,540 --> 00:26:57,240
なんか...
Wait...

719
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,640
これ飛んでる！
It skips!

720
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,540
飛んでるのじゃ。
It really does skip.

721
00:26:59,140 --> 00:27:00,340
これ何だっけ？
What was this called again?

722
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:01,440
富士山とか？山とか？
Mt. Fuji? Or mountains?

723
00:27:01,140 --> 00:27:02,540
途切れてる！
It's disconnected!

724
00:27:02,740 --> 00:27:07,840
え、大分途切れてるよ。起点から終、終点が...
Woah, a huge chunk is missing. From the start to the ter... terminal point...

725
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:09,540
山がすごいのかな？
Maybe the mountains are too rugged?

726
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:10,940
これ何だ？
What is this?

727
00:27:10,440 --> 00:27:11,640
なんじゃろ？
I wonder what it is.

728
00:27:11,740 --> 00:27:12,740
なんだ...
What could...

729
00:27:12,740 --> 00:27:16,540
複雑な道、分断されてる？飛び地？
A complicated route... Is it divided? An enclave?

730
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:19,340
何が... なんでこんな飛んでるんじゃろ？
Why... Why does it skip like this?

731
00:27:18,840 --> 00:27:21,140
未完成？そんなこともある？
Incomplete? Can that happen?

732
00:27:20,640 --> 00:27:21,440
もしかして...
Could it be...

733
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:25,340
え〜こういうこともあるの？別の道路じゃないんだね、しかも。
Huh, that can happen? And it's not even a different route!

734
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:27,840
474、これはレア。
Route 474, this is a Rare.

735
00:27:27,540 --> 00:27:28,840
なんで、なんでだろう？
Why? Why would that be?

736
00:27:28,140 --> 00:27:29,340
未開通...
Unopened...

737
00:27:29,340 --> 00:27:30,840
なんで分断されてるんじゃろ？
Why is it severed?

738
00:27:30,340 --> 00:27:31,440
ワープ！
It warps!

739
00:27:31,440 --> 00:27:34,740
474です。謎が深まる。
Route 474. The mystery deepens.

740
00:27:35,340 --> 00:27:38,740
この辺アルプスとかある辺？南アルプスとかある辺？
Is this where the Alps are? Around the Southern Alps?

741
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:40,140
え、でも長野だからね。
Well, it is Nagano.

742
00:27:39,940 --> 00:27:43,640
やっぱ山によって、流石にこの山は無理や！って...
Because of the mountains, they must've been like, "No way we can cross this mountain!"...

743
00:27:43,140 --> 00:27:46,040
ここはトンネルが難しいとかかな？
Maybe building a tunnel here was too difficult?

744
00:27:45,040 --> 00:27:47,540
国道どころじゃない、みたいな。感じなんかの？
Like, "Forget a national highway!" Is that it?

745
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:48,840
できてない感じなんじゃろか。
Could it be under construction?

746
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:50,240
トンネル作ってます？
Are they building a tunnel?

747
00:27:49,840 --> 00:27:50,940
へえ〜
Huh...

748
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:51,640
ん〜
Hmm...

749
00:27:51,740 --> 00:27:55,140
へえ〜！「出た、青崩峠」って。
Whoa! Chat says, "There it is, Aokuzure Pass!"

750
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:56,440
青崩峠？
Aokuzure Pass?

751
00:27:56,340 --> 00:27:57,840
かなり有名な...
It's a pretty famous...

752
00:27:57,840 --> 00:27:59,540
へえ〜
Ooh...

753
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:03,640
そう、調査が必要ですね、これは。めらちゃん。
Yeah, this definitely warrants an investigation, Mera-chan.

754
00:28:03,540 --> 00:28:04,640
調査したい！
I want to investigate!

755
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:09,140
さっきの鳥取... 兵庫から鳥取のとこ近かったけど、違った。
The one before from Tottori... Hyogo to Tottori was close, but different.

756
00:28:08,040 --> 00:28:09,240
あ、近かった？
Oh, was it close?

757
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:13,740
近いけど、重なってはいないくらいかも。
It's close, but maybe not quite overlapping.

758
00:28:13,540 --> 00:28:18,140
はいはいはいはい、本当だ。でもなんかどっか交差して... あ、してないか。
Right, right. You're right. But does it intersect somewhere... Ah, maybe not.

759
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:19,140
ギリしてない？
Barely not?

760
00:28:18,940 --> 00:28:20,040
してないか。
Guess not.

761
00:28:19,940 --> 00:28:21,440
してないかな、くらい。
Looks like it barely doesn't.

762
00:28:21,040 --> 00:28:22,340
はいはいはい。
Right, right.

763
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:24,840
ちょっと、意外に近く見えて近くないことあり。
Surprisingly, they can look close without actually being close.

764
00:28:24,740 --> 00:28:25,840
ありけり。
Verily so.

765
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:28,540
え〜道って... え、日本広くてワロタ。
Roads are so... Wow, Japan is huge, lol.

766
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:30,340
日本広いで！
Japan really is huge!

767
00:28:30,140 --> 00:28:31,540
広いのじゃ！
It's gigantic!

768
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:31,940
はい。
Yes.

769
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:32,840
それでは、
And now,

770
00:28:32,740 --> 00:28:33,640
どうぞ。
Go ahead.

771
00:28:33,340 --> 00:28:37,040
次の道も見ていきますのじゃー！
Let's check out the next roads!

772
00:28:36,840 --> 00:28:38,040
お願いします。
Go for it!

773
00:28:37,740 --> 00:28:39,440
まずはこちら。
First up is this one.

774
00:28:39,340 --> 00:28:39,940
お。
Oh.

775
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:40,840
栃木。
Tochigi.

776
00:28:40,840 --> 00:28:42,540
122号。
Route 122.

777
00:28:42,540 --> 00:28:45,140
122。日光から...
Route 122. From Nikko to...

778
00:28:44,840 --> 00:28:46,340
日光から...
From Nikko to...

779
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:48,340
え、東京都豊島区！
What, Toshima Ward, Tokyo!

780
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:49,340
え、東京まで！？
Whoa, all the way to Tokyo?!

781
00:28:49,140 --> 00:28:51,140
池袋まで行けるんですか？
You can take this all the way to Ikebukuro?

782
00:28:51,240 --> 00:28:52,840
じゃあ結構...
Then that's pretty...

783
00:28:53,040 --> 00:28:56,840
結構長いね。163キロ。
It's pretty long. 163 kilometers.

784
00:28:56,540 --> 00:28:57,840
長いな。
That is long.

785
00:28:57,840 --> 00:29:01,440
へえ〜じゃあ東京から日光、この道で行けるんだ。
Wow, so you can go from Tokyo to Nikko on this road!

786
00:29:00,840 --> 00:29:04,840
へえ〜こ、高速？高速とかじゃなくて行ける？
Huh... An ex-expressway? You can go without taking an expressway?

787
00:29:03,440 --> 00:29:04,440
普通...
Normal...

788
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:05,640
うん。
Yeah.

789
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:06,340
へえ〜
Wow...

790
00:29:06,140 --> 00:29:08,440
下道で行くならこの道なのかな？
I guess this is the route if you take surface streets.

791
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:13,740
じゃあこの道、122を見つければ、とりあえず日光までは旅行に行けちゃうよという。
So if you find Route 122, you can basically just travel all the way to Nikko!

792
00:29:13,440 --> 00:29:16,540
日光街道？へえ〜
Nikko Kaido? Wow...

793
00:29:16,540 --> 00:29:19,340
みんなのコメント見つつ... へえ〜
Reading everyone's comments... Wow...

794
00:29:18,740 --> 00:29:20,640
有識者がいっぱいいらっしゃる。
There are so many experts in chat!

795
00:29:20,340 --> 00:29:21,140
ね。
Truly.

796
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:24,340
お、結構長いね。埼玉を越えていきます。
Oh, it's quite long. It cuts straight through Saitama.

797
00:29:24,140 --> 00:29:27,840
うんうんうん。あ、でも結構途中で山にぶつかる予感。
Yeah, yeah. Ah, but I have a feeling it runs into mountains along the way.

798
00:29:27,740 --> 00:29:30,640
日光街道122号。
Nikko Kaido, Route 122.

799
00:29:30,340 --> 00:29:31,340
へえ〜
Huh...

800
00:29:31,140 --> 00:29:33,640
関東平野から北上して、
Heading north from the Kanto Plain...

801
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:34,140
いいね。
Nice.

802
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:38,340
山の辺にぶつかって... 日光じゃから多いよね、その辺。
Hitting the mountain area... Since it's Nikko, there are plenty of them around there.

803
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:38,640
うん。
Yeah.

804
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:39,640
なるほど。
I see.

805
00:29:39,540 --> 00:29:42,940
122号。うわ、これ数字で覚えるの難しそう。
Route 122. Man, remembering these by number seems so tough!

806
00:29:42,040 --> 00:29:45,040
2号。いやムズい！もうちょっと無理だもんね。
Route 122. So hard! It feels almost impossible.

807
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:48,040
覚え... 覚えるのはちょっとやってくしか... なんかカルタとかにしてくれたら、
Rememb... The only way to remember is through practice... If they turned it into karuta cards or something,

808
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:48,940
確かに！
True!

809
00:29:48,740 --> 00:29:50,640
そう！「122！」つって、こう...
Exactly! You shout "122!" and then, like...

810
00:29:49,940 --> 00:29:51,740
バーン！みたいな。
SLAM! Like that.

811
00:29:51,140 --> 00:29:53,840
みたいなので覚えられるかもしれないけど、こっちは...
We might remember it that way, but just like this...

812
00:29:53,340 --> 00:29:55,840
競技、競技的な感じで。
Like a competitive sport!

813
00:29:55,340 --> 00:29:58,440
眺めるのじゃちょっと初見で覚えるのはむずそうなのじゃ。
Just looking at them makes it tough to memorize on the first try.

814
00:29:58,340 --> 00:30:00,040
はあ〜おもろ。
Haha, so fun.

815
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:01,340
次！
Next!

816
00:30:01,048 --> 00:30:02,428
えい、よいしょ。
There we go.

817
00:30:02,428 --> 00:30:03,828
富山...
Toyama...

818
00:30:03,308 --> 00:30:04,508
富山きた！
Here comes Toyama!

819
00:30:04,508 --> 00:30:05,748
岐阜？
Gifu?

820
00:30:05,748 --> 00:30:07,048
はいはいはいはい。
Right, right, right...

821
00:30:07,048 --> 00:30:09,548
え、ここもまた結構過酷な...
Wait, this looks like another pretty harsh...

822
00:30:09,548 --> 00:30:11,948
うん、山間だよね、絶対ね。
Yeah, it's definitely mountainous, for sure.

823
00:30:11,948 --> 00:30:12,848
ねー。
Yeah.

824
00:30:13,048 --> 00:30:15,548
しかも結構攻めた南北...
And it cuts pretty aggressively north to south...

825
00:30:15,548 --> 00:30:17,248
これー。
Look at this...

826
00:30:17,248 --> 00:30:19,448
187？長めじゃ。
187? That's on the longer side.

827
00:30:19,048 --> 00:30:20,448
187。
187.

828
00:30:20,448 --> 00:30:21,948
なかなか長いのじゃ。
It's quite long.

829
00:30:21,948 --> 00:30:25,448
岐阜に入る、そこの...あ、なんかちょっとさ、途切れてない？
Entering Gifu, right there... Wait, isn't it cut off a bit?

830
00:30:25,448 --> 00:30:27,348
確かに！途切れてる！
You're right! It is cut off!

831
00:30:27,348 --> 00:30:28,448
そこ...
Right there...

832
00:30:27,748 --> 00:30:29,948
いや、やばいからか。山がやばすぎるからか？
Maybe because it's too treacherous. Are the mountains too crazy?

833
00:30:29,948 --> 00:30:34,248
どうなんだろう？え、なんでそこ繋がってないんだろう？気になる！
I wonder why? Why isn't it connected there? Now I'm curious!

834
00:30:32,248 --> 00:30:33,448
なんじゃろ？
What could it be?

835
00:30:34,248 --> 00:30:36,448
え、でも水とか、ダ、ダムとか...
Wait, could it be water, or a d-dam...?

836
00:30:36,448 --> 00:30:38,448
トンネル？なんだろう？あ、確かに、そっか。
A tunnel? What is it? Ah, true, that could be it.

837
00:30:38,448 --> 00:30:40,348
湖、ダムとかありそうな予感。
I have a feeling there might be a lake or a dam.

838
00:30:40,348 --> 00:30:42,248
そういう可能性もあるね。
That's definitely a possibility.

839
00:30:42,248 --> 00:30:43,548
なんじゃろ？
What is it?

840
00:30:43,548 --> 00:30:45,848
白川郷あたり？
Around Shirakawa-go?

841
00:30:45,548 --> 00:30:46,848
へえー。
Hmm, I see.

842
00:30:47,048 --> 00:30:50,048
もうここはもう、絶対にやばそうな道。
This road definitely looks insane.

843
00:30:50,048 --> 00:30:52,248
はいはいはいはいはい。
Right, right, right.

844
00:30:51,548 --> 00:30:53,048
後ろで見ると...
Looking at the back...

845
00:30:52,548 --> 00:30:54,248
調査が必要かもしれん。
We might need to investigate this.

846
00:30:54,248 --> 00:30:57,848
えー、ここを突っ切るんじゃ。わしだったら怖いから山回っちゃうな。
Whoa, it cuts straight through here. If it were me, I'd be scared and go around the mountains.

847
00:30:56,248 --> 00:30:57,248
きゃー。
Eek!

848
00:30:57,848 --> 00:30:59,248
怖いね。
That is scary.

849
00:30:59,248 --> 00:31:01,648
この道ちょっと怖そうだよ。
This road looks pretty scary.

850
00:31:01,648 --> 00:31:03,148
いや、怖そう。
Yeah, looks scary.

851
00:31:03,148 --> 00:31:05,348
なかなかチャレンジャーな...
Quite an adventurous...

852
00:31:04,748 --> 00:31:05,848
ねえ。
Yeah.

853
00:31:05,348 --> 00:31:09,548
道の予感。山がね、いっぱい。ひゃー。
Kind of road, I feel. Lots of mountains. Whoa!

854
00:31:09,548 --> 00:31:11,548
次のカード！
Next card!

855
00:31:11,548 --> 00:31:14,248
はい。じゃじゃーん、1号！
Alright. Ta-da! Route 1!

856
00:31:14,248 --> 00:31:16,548
おー！きたー！
Ooh! It's here!

857
00:31:16,548 --> 00:31:17,848
本命じゃ！
The real deal!

858
00:31:17,848 --> 00:31:19,848
1号線じゃん！
It's Route 1!

859
00:31:19,048 --> 00:31:20,448
本命じゃ。
The main event.

860
00:31:20,448 --> 00:31:23,048
えー、東京から大阪に向かっていて...
Yeah, running from Tokyo towards Osaka...

861
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:25,748
日本橋からね。
Starting from Nihonbashi, right?

862
00:31:25,048 --> 00:31:26,048
こう。
Like this.

863
00:31:26,048 --> 00:31:31,848
なんか国道は東京を起点にして1号からこう、1、2って...
National highways start from Tokyo as the origin, going Route 1, 2...

864
00:31:31,848 --> 00:31:36,348
2が西で、3が九州みたいなの...
Route 2 heads west, Route 3 is in Kyushu, that kind of thing...

865
00:31:36,348 --> 00:31:39,248
おー！すごい。だから一気に...
Ooh! Wow. So in one go...

866
00:31:39,248 --> 00:31:44,348
東京から西まで行く道の一番大事な道。
The most important road heading from Tokyo out west.

867
00:31:39,548 --> 00:31:41,548
西を攻めて...
Covering the west...

868
00:31:44,348 --> 00:31:46,348
最初の一号なのじゃ。
It's the very first Route 1.

869
00:31:46,348 --> 00:31:48,448
はー、東海道きちゃー！
Ah, the Tokaido is here!

870
00:31:48,048 --> 00:31:49,348
へえー。
Heeh...

871
00:31:49,348 --> 00:31:50,848
お世話になってます。
We owe you a lot!

872
00:31:50,848 --> 00:31:52,548
765km。
765 kilometers.

873
00:31:52,548 --> 00:31:55,448
え、これが一番長いんだよね、きっと。どうなんだろ？
Wait, this has got to be the longest one, right? Or is it?

874
00:31:55,448 --> 00:31:56,748
あ、一番長いかも？どう？
Ah, maybe it is the longest? How is it?

875
00:31:56,748 --> 00:31:58,448
なが...もっと長いの...
Long... Is there a longer one...?

876
00:31:58,448 --> 00:31:59,748
もっと長いの、あるのかな？
Could there be an even longer one?

877
00:31:59,748 --> 00:32:02,348
でも流石に結構東京から大阪までは長...
Though honestly, Tokyo to Osaka is pretty lo--

878
00:32:02,348 --> 00:32:07,048
長いですよ。これ下道で1号で行くとどれくらいかかるんだろ？
It is long! If you take local roads on Route 1, how long would it take?

879
00:32:07,548 --> 00:32:11,048
あんま車乗んないから想像がつかない。
I don't drive much, so I can't even imagine.

880
00:32:08,448 --> 00:32:11,448
4だっけ？あ、4の方が長いんだ。
Was it Route 4? Ah, Route 4 is longer.

881
00:32:11,448 --> 00:32:14,448
1より4か。4号線が一番長い。
Route 4 over Route 1, huh? Route 4 is the longest.

882
00:32:14,448 --> 00:32:18,048
あれか、あの、東北？青森からの...
Is that the one in Tohoku? From Aomori...

883
00:32:15,348 --> 00:32:17,848
東北。そうそうそうそう。
Tohoku. Exactly, yeah.

884
00:32:18,048 --> 00:32:20,848
4号線が一番か。
Route 4 is the longest, huh?

885
00:32:20,848 --> 00:32:22,348
のじゃ、長い。
Indeed, that's long.

886
00:32:22,348 --> 00:32:25,048
ひー。13時間くらいで行けるらしいですよ。
Yikes. Apparently it takes about 13 hours.

887
00:32:25,048 --> 00:32:27,548
え？それでも13時間！
What? Even so, 13 hours!

888
00:32:27,548 --> 00:32:29,048
大変だー。
That's intense.

889
00:32:29,048 --> 00:32:31,248
下道ってめっちゃ大変なのじゃ。
Local roads are seriously grueling!

890
00:32:30,348 --> 00:32:32,048
大変じゃー。
Grueling indeed!

891
00:32:32,048 --> 00:32:33,448
はい。次。
Alright, next.

892
00:32:33,448 --> 00:32:35,048
次。お、これは...
Next. Oh, this is...

893
00:32:35,048 --> 00:32:37,748
439ってもしかして...
Could 439 be...

894
00:32:37,048 --> 00:32:38,548
あーーー！きたー！
Ahhh! It's here!

895
00:32:37,748 --> 00:32:41,248
AZKiの推し酷の「与作」じゃん！
It's my favorite 'cruel road', Yosaku!

896
00:32:41,248 --> 00:32:42,248
「与作」！
Yosaku!

897
00:32:42,248 --> 00:32:43,548
与作！
Yosaku!

898
00:32:42,848 --> 00:32:44,748
苦しいという道。苦しい道。
A road written with the kanji for 'suffering'.

899
00:32:44,748 --> 00:32:49,448
日本三大酷道と書いて、書く酷道の方だ！
One of Japan's Top Three 'Kokudō', written with the kanji for 'cruel'!

900
00:32:49,448 --> 00:32:51,048
与作きたー！
Yosaku is here!

901
00:32:51,048 --> 00:32:55,048
これ、四国のね、徳島から高知を...
This one in Shikoku, from Tokushima to Kochi...

902
00:32:51,448 --> 00:32:52,648
徳島から...
From Tokushima...

903
00:32:55,048 --> 00:32:57,248
すごいね、こう見ると。
It's amazing looking at it like this.

904
00:32:56,548 --> 00:32:57,548
ねえ。
Yeah.

905
00:32:57,248 --> 00:32:59,248
四国をこんな横に突っ切る...
Cutting horizontally across Shikoku like this...

906
00:32:59,248 --> 00:33:01,648
横に突っ切って、しかも...
It cuts horizontally, and on top of that...

907
00:33:00,348 --> 00:33:01,848
しかもド山。
And it's total mountains!

908
00:33:01,648 --> 00:33:04,248
そうだよ！一番山だよね、そこ。
Exactly! It's the most mountainous part!

909
00:33:02,048 --> 00:33:04,048
山脈が通ってるところ。
Right where the mountain range runs.

910
00:33:04,248 --> 00:33:07,548
そう、四国の一番の、あの、山々しているところ。
Yeah, the most ruggedly mountainous part of Shikoku.

911
00:33:07,548 --> 00:33:09,648
すごい、すごい、すごい、すごい。
Incredible, incredible, incredible...

912
00:33:08,548 --> 00:33:09,848
すごーい。
Amazing.

913
00:33:09,648 --> 00:33:11,448
過酷なのじゃー。
It's brutal!

914
00:33:11,448 --> 00:33:14,248
いや、ここはすごいよ。
No really, this place is incredible.

915
00:33:13,648 --> 00:33:15,048
へえーー。
Wow...

916
00:33:14,248 --> 00:33:19,548
いや、もう、なんか全然ここ大丈夫かな、ここ落ちたら死ぬな、みたいな。
Like, 'Is this really safe? If I fall off here, I'm dead' kind of vibes.

917
00:33:19,548 --> 00:33:23,348
えー、やばい。高度も結構あるんじゃろか？
Whoa, insane. I wonder if the altitude is pretty high too?

918
00:33:23,348 --> 00:33:28,048
高いし、あの、本当車が一台通れるかギリギリの...
It's high up, and the road is barely wide enough for one car to pass...

919
00:33:28,048 --> 00:33:29,448
道も狭い。
The roads are narrow too.

920
00:33:29,448 --> 00:33:31,048
道もある。
There are sections like that.

921
00:33:30,448 --> 00:33:32,048
へえー。
Hoo.

922
00:33:32,048 --> 00:33:34,848
でもなんか四国に道を作ろうってなった時に、
But when they decided to build roads in Shikoku...

923
00:33:34,848 --> 00:33:39,848
ここにわし道置けないかも、怖くて。ビビっちゃって。
I don't think I could've laid a road here, I'd be too scared. I'd totally chicken out.

924
00:33:39,848 --> 00:33:41,248
置けないかも。
You might not have.

925
00:33:39,848 --> 00:33:42,048
ちょ、流石にちょっとずつ回る...
I'd have to go around little by little...

926
00:33:42,048 --> 00:33:44,248
え、だって、あの、この辺だけでも結構...
Because even just around here...

927
00:33:44,248 --> 00:33:47,548
さっきも高知のカードとかあったから見たけど、
Earlier we saw a Kochi card too...

928
00:33:47,548 --> 00:33:51,348
ここだけでも結構なかなか攻めた道じゃなって思ったのに、
Even just this part seemed like a pretty daring road, but...

929
00:33:51,348 --> 00:33:53,448
ここからっていう...
Starting from here...

930
00:33:52,548 --> 00:33:54,048
いや、そうだよ。
Yeah, exactly.

931
00:33:53,448 --> 00:33:57,248
その、そう、この本当に中間ぐらい、
Right in the middle section there...

932
00:33:57,248 --> 00:33:59,748
GeoGuessrで行きましたけど、
I ended up there in GeoGuessr once, but...

933
00:33:59,748 --> 00:34:01,648
いや、これはドライビングテクニックも必要です。
Man, you definitely need serious driving skills for this.

934
00:34:01,648 --> 00:34:04,548
いやー、怖いじゃろうな。え、しかもこういうのって、道って車だけじゃなくてバイクとか...
Man, it must be terrifying. And roads like this aren't just for cars, but motorcycles too...

935
00:34:05,548 --> 00:34:09,448
あ、バイク！いや、バイクの方が危ないかもな。
Ah, motorcycles! Actually, a motorcycle might be even more dangerous.

936
00:34:06,548 --> 00:34:07,648
バイク...
Motorcycles...

937
00:34:09,448 --> 00:34:13,748
怖いかも。だって、あの、鉄にさ、守られていないんじゃろ？車じゃったらさ、
That might be scarier. I mean, you're not protected by steel, right? With a car...

938
00:34:14,248 --> 00:34:17,448
あの、まあ、風を直に浴びることはないから、
Well, you don't take the full brunt of the wind, so...

939
00:34:15,348 --> 00:34:16,848
うん。ま、確かにね。
Yeah, true.

940
00:34:17,448 --> 00:34:20,448
ちょっと怖さ軽減されるかもしれんのじゃけど、
The fear might be a bit lessened, but...

941
00:34:18,648 --> 00:34:19,648
あー。
Ah...

942
00:34:20,448 --> 00:34:23,448
バイクでここちょっと、なかなか...
Doing this on a motorcycle is pretty...

943
00:34:23,448 --> 00:34:27,148
めらちゃん、この道、普通に電柱ないから。
Mera-chan, this road literally doesn't have utility poles.

944
00:34:27,148 --> 00:34:28,348
え？
Huh?

945
00:34:28,348 --> 00:34:30,048
わしは何で決...
How am I supposed to deter...

946
00:34:29,048 --> 00:34:30,848
電柱...電柱ない区間あるんで。
There are sections with no utility poles at all.

947
00:34:30,848 --> 00:34:33,448
ええ、そう、もう明るい時に絶対行ってください。
So please, definitely only go during daylight hours.

948
00:34:33,448 --> 00:34:36,348
怖い。え、じゃあもう分かんないかも。
Terrifying! Wait, then you can't tell where you are at all!

949
00:34:36,348 --> 00:34:41,448
いや、そう、四国のね、この辺のね、山はね、電柱ないから本当にね、見分けつかない感じ...
Yeah, the mountains around here in Shikoku have no poles, so it's truly impossible to tell apart...

950
00:34:41,448 --> 00:34:45,248
そうなんだよ！くそー！難しいよね。
Exactly! Damn it! It's so tough, right?

951
00:34:41,848 --> 00:34:43,548
え、草...
Wait, the grass...

952
00:34:44,048 --> 00:34:45,848
難しいのじゃ。
It's so difficult.

953
00:34:45,248 --> 00:34:47,748
植生、植生からゲスしないとね。
You have to guess from the vegetation, the flora.

954
00:34:47,748 --> 00:34:49,348
え、高知のこの辺の植生分かんない...
Wait, I don't know the flora in this part of Kochi...

955
00:34:49,348 --> 00:34:51,148
うん、そう、意外と難しい。
Yeah, it's surprisingly tricky.

956
00:34:51,148 --> 00:34:52,348
難しい！
It is tricky!

957
00:34:51,848 --> 00:34:52,848
はい。
Okay.

958
00:34:52,348 --> 00:34:54,648
次なのじゃ！えー、355号。
On to the next! Route 355.

959
00:34:54,648 --> 00:34:55,848
お、355。
Oh, 355.

960
00:34:55,848 --> 00:34:58,048
お、千葉から茨城。
Oh, from Chiba to Ibaraki.

961
00:34:58,048 --> 00:34:59,548
から？おーー。
To? Ooh.

962
00:34:58,448 --> 00:35:00,048
茨城から...
From Ibaraki...

963
00:34:59,548 --> 00:35:02,348
霞ヶ浦？これ。
Kasumigaura? Is this it?

964
00:35:01,648 --> 00:35:02,848
うん、のはず。
Yeah, should be.

965
00:35:02,348 --> 00:35:03,448
のはず。
Should be.

966
00:35:03,448 --> 00:35:04,848
おー、こう...
Ooh, like this...

967
00:35:04,248 --> 00:35:05,636
すごい、これじゃあさ、
Wow, so with this...

968
00:35:05,636 --> 00:35:07,472
見えるのかな？この
Can you see this...

969
00:35:07,472 --> 00:35:08,836
湖というか
...lake, or whatever it is?

970
00:35:08,836 --> 00:35:09,736
確かに。
True.

971
00:35:09,736 --> 00:35:14,136
見えそうな予感。この辺めっちゃ平野じゃから、それ以外に...
I feel like you can. Around here is mostly plains, so besides that...

972
00:35:13,836 --> 00:35:16,136
見えそう。いい道、なんか。
You probably can. It seems like a nice road.

973
00:35:14,436 --> 00:35:15,636
見えるものが...
There's not much else to see...

974
00:35:16,836 --> 00:35:22,936
なんかさ、こう、朝とか夕方とかさ、日が入ったら絶対綺麗な感じ。
Like, in the morning or evening when the sun hits it, it must be gorgeous.

975
00:35:22,936 --> 00:35:29,436
綺麗じゃし、多分、かなり安全めな道。酷くない道かも。ぼこぼこしてなさそう。
It would be pretty, and it's probably a pretty safe road. Not a 'cruel road'. Doesn't look bumpy.

976
00:35:29,436 --> 00:35:31,136
確かに、平野だからね。
True, since it's on plains.

977
00:35:31,136 --> 00:35:33,136
大平野の道じゃから。
Because it's a road across the great plains.

978
00:35:33,136 --> 00:35:35,436
いいね。なんか結構枝分かれしてんね、途中で。
Nice. And it branches off quite a bit midway.

979
00:35:35,436 --> 00:35:37,536
え、途中で止まってる。なんでなんじゃろ？
Huh, it just stops midway. Why is that?

980
00:35:37,536 --> 00:35:39,636
えー、珍しい。今までにない感じ。
Ooh, that's rare. Not like anything we've seen so far.

981
00:35:39,636 --> 00:35:43,836
でもやっぱこういう道って自然物に沿って作られてて面白いな。川とか湖とか山とか。
Still, it's so interesting how roads like this are built along natural features. Like rivers, lakes, and mountains.

982
00:35:43,836 --> 00:35:46,136
ねえ、そうだね。
Yeah, definitely.

983
00:35:46,136 --> 00:35:48,436
いいですね、通ってみたいね。
It looks nice, I'd love to drive it.

984
00:35:48,636 --> 00:35:49,836
ここな。
Right here, huh.

985
00:35:49,836 --> 00:35:50,936
そこ。茨城県。
There. Ibaraki Prefecture.

986
00:35:50,936 --> 00:35:53,436
分かりやすい。なんかちょうど県の境目って感じ。
That's easy to spot. Looks like it's right on the prefectural border.

987
00:35:53,436 --> 00:35:54,436
ほんとだ。
You're right.

988
00:35:55,136 --> 00:35:56,836
よし、そして次。
Alright, on to the next one!

989
00:35:56,836 --> 00:35:57,836
おっ。あ！
Oh! Ah!

990
00:35:58,436 --> 00:35:59,636
これはお、
Wait, is this...

991
00:35:59,636 --> 00:36:02,136
また321。
321 again.

992
00:36:02,136 --> 00:36:03,636
あ、321だ！
Ah, it's 321!

993
00:36:03,636 --> 00:36:04,636
再び？
Again?

994
00:36:04,636 --> 00:36:05,636
再びだ。
Again!

995
00:36:05,636 --> 00:36:07,436
だんだん被ってきたぞ。
We're starting to get duplicates!

996
00:36:07,436 --> 00:36:08,836
被ってきたのじゃ。
Duplicates have arrived!

997
00:36:08,836 --> 00:36:11,136
やっぱランダムじゃとね、こういうことが。
That's what happens with random packs.

998
00:36:10,636 --> 00:36:12,136
そう、こういうこともある。
Yeah, that happens.

999
00:36:12,136 --> 00:36:14,636
おっ、ああっ！次はなんと...
Oh, ah! Next up is...

1000
00:36:14,836 --> 00:36:16,436
スーパーレア！
Super Rare!

1001
00:36:16,436 --> 00:36:18,636
スーパーレアきたーー！
Super Rare pulled!!

1002
00:36:18,636 --> 00:36:21,136
まさかのスーパーレア！え、何これ！？
An unexpected Super Rare! Wait, what is this?!

1003
00:36:21,136 --> 00:36:24,436
なんだ、説明...「4連おにぎり」
What does it say? "4-in-a-row Onigiri".

1004
00:36:24,436 --> 00:36:25,436
ほう。
Oho.

1005
00:36:25,436 --> 00:36:27,436
きたーー！「4連おにぎり」？
Yes! "4-in-a-row Onigiri"?

1006
00:36:27,436 --> 00:36:29,136
なんだなんだ？交差点に...
What's that, what's that? At an intersection...

1007
00:36:29,136 --> 00:36:36,636
福井県敦賀市内の交差点にある4つの国道が重複している区間に設置されている標識で、
"A sign installed along a section in Tsuruga City, Fukui Prefecture where four national highways overlap,

1008
00:36:36,636 --> 00:36:38,836
「4連おにぎり」という愛称で親しまれている。
affectionately known as the '4-in-a-row Onigiri'"...

1009
00:36:38,836 --> 00:36:41,436
あ、「4連おにぎり」、これか！
Ah, this is the "4-in-a-row Onigiri"!

1010
00:36:41,436 --> 00:36:42,636
知ってるんですか？
You know about this?

1011
00:36:42,636 --> 00:36:48,136
え、なんか、この4つ並ぶってなかなかないから、レアな...
Well, having four of them lined up like this is super rare...

1012
00:36:46,136 --> 00:36:47,136
はいはい。
Right, right.

1013
00:36:48,136 --> 00:36:49,836
すごーい！
Amazing!

1014
00:36:49,836 --> 00:36:52,636
なかなかないっていうのはどう、なんか県道と...
What do you mean by rare? Like compared to prefectural roads...

1015
00:36:52,136 --> 00:36:54,436
ひょ、標識として！標識として。
As a sign! As a signpost.

1016
00:36:54,436 --> 00:36:55,636
標識？
A sign?

1017
00:36:55,636 --> 00:36:57,636
なんか多分、こ、この、こんな感じで...
Like, probably... vertically like this...

1018
00:36:57,636 --> 00:36:58,636
あ、縦に？
Oh, stacked vertically?

1019
00:36:58,636 --> 00:37:00,836
そうそうそうそうそうそう。
Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

1020
00:36:59,636 --> 00:37:01,136
へー。
I see.

1021
00:37:00,636 --> 00:37:02,636
おにぎり、おにぎり...
Onigiri, onigiri...

1022
00:37:02,136 --> 00:37:06,436
あ、そうか。あの、国道の標識が三角だからってことじゃ。
Ah, right! It's called that because the national highway signs are shaped like triangles!

1023
00:37:06,436 --> 00:37:09,636
そうそうそうそう、おにぎりと言います、この形を。
Exactly! They call this shield shape "onigiri".

1024
00:37:09,136 --> 00:37:11,136
なるほど。青とかは違うからな。
I see. Prefectural road signs are blue hexagons, so they're different.

1025
00:37:11,136 --> 00:37:19,636
この標識は8号の上に27号が配置されているのも特徴で、このような並び順は珍しく、愛好家の間では「下克上」と呼ばれている。
"Another feature is that Route 27 is placed above Route 8; this ordering is unusual and is called 'Gekokujo' among fans."

1026
00:37:19,136 --> 00:37:21,636
あ、確かに！順番で上から8、27...
Ah, true! Usually the order would be 8, then 27...

1027
00:37:21,636 --> 00:37:24,636
なんでだろう？8、普通は8から置きたいけど...
Why is that? Route 8... normally you'd want to put 8 first.

1028
00:37:24,636 --> 00:37:26,136
下克上なんじゃ。
It's an upset!

1029
00:37:26,136 --> 00:37:29,136
えー！こんな特殊、特殊な感じね。
Whoa! That is a really special one.

1030
00:37:29,136 --> 00:37:34,636
なんか、と、特殊な、スーパーレアの国道があるわけではなく、国道の...
It's not that there's a Super Rare national highway route itself,

1031
00:37:33,136 --> 00:37:34,136
愛好家...
"Among fans..."

1032
00:37:34,636 --> 00:37:37,636
なんか豆知識を教えてくれる感じなんじゃな。
it's more like it teaches you national highway trivia.

1033
00:37:37,636 --> 00:37:39,636
はいはい。いや、いいですね！
Right, right. Wow, this is so cool!

1034
00:37:38,636 --> 00:37:39,636
へー。
Wow.

1035
00:37:39,636 --> 00:37:43,636
すごい。これはゲスしたくなるな。
Amazing. This totally makes me want to guess it in GeoGuessr.

1036
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:49,636
確かに言われてみれば、あの青看板とかで4方向に国道あるの珍しいかも。
Come to think of it, having national highways in all four directions on a guide sign is pretty rare.

1037
00:37:49,636 --> 00:37:52,436
大体県道と国道とかの交差点だったりするから。
Usually an intersection is between a national highway and prefectural roads.

1038
00:37:51,636 --> 00:37:53,136
そうだねー。
That's true.

1039
00:37:53,436 --> 00:37:54,636
なるほど。
Makes sense.

1040
00:37:54,636 --> 00:37:57,136
へー、これがスーパーレアでございます。
Ooh, so this is what a Super Rare is!

1041
00:37:57,136 --> 00:37:58,636
あ、後ろどうなってんだ？
Ah, what does the back look like?

1042
00:37:58,636 --> 00:37:59,636
ん？
Hm?

1043
00:37:59,636 --> 00:38:02,136
4連おにぎり
"4-in-a-row Onigiri".

1044
00:38:02,136 --> 00:38:04,136
煽りすぎるだろ。
That's so blatant!

1045
00:38:03,636 --> 00:38:05,636
へー。これ公式応募？
Heh. Was that officially submitted?

1046
00:38:05,636 --> 00:38:08,136
愛称ですね。
It's just a nickname.

1047
00:38:07,636 --> 00:38:09,636
愛称。へー。
A nickname. Oho.

1048
00:38:08,436 --> 00:38:09,636
愛称、愛称。
A nickname, just a nickname.

1049
00:38:09,636 --> 00:38:11,636
誰がつけるんじゃ、こういうのな。
Who even comes up with these names?

1050
00:38:11,636 --> 00:38:16,636
国道がね、好きなね、マニアのオタクの中では有名な。
It's famous among hardcore national highway enthusiasts.

1051
00:38:16,636 --> 00:38:18,136
ふーん。
Hmm.

1052
00:38:18,136 --> 00:38:19,636
よし、いくか。
Alright, let's keep going.

1053
00:38:19,636 --> 00:38:22,436
まだ行くぜ。たくさんあるのじゃ。え、なんか面白い。
Still plenty left! There are tons. Oh, this is fun.

1054
00:38:22,436 --> 00:38:24,136
でもそろそろ被ってきた。
Though duplicates are starting to show up.

1055
00:38:24,136 --> 00:38:25,136
おっ。
Oh.

1056
00:38:25,136 --> 00:38:26,436
322。
Route 322.

1057
00:38:26,436 --> 00:38:28,136
はいはいはい。見ましたね、これ。322。
Right, right. We've seen this one. Route 322.

1058
00:38:28,136 --> 00:38:30,136
一番最初に見たやつじゃん。
That was the very first one we opened!

1059
00:38:30,136 --> 00:38:32,136
322でございます。
Here is Route 322.

1060
00:38:32,136 --> 00:38:33,436
ふんふんふん。
Yep, yep, yep.

1061
00:38:33,436 --> 00:38:35,636
一応スーパーレアだけ、あ、そっか。
I guess we'll keep the Super Rare... Ah, right.

1062
00:38:34,636 --> 00:38:36,636
確かにな。
For sure.

1063
00:38:36,136 --> 00:38:37,636
引けましたね。
We actually pulled one!

1064
00:38:37,636 --> 00:38:39,636
これスーパーレアね。
This is our Super Rare.

1065
00:38:40,636 --> 00:38:42,636
はい。291。
Alright, Route 291.

1066
00:38:42,636 --> 00:38:43,836
ふんふんふん。
Mhm, mhm.

1067
00:38:43,836 --> 00:38:48,636
群馬から新潟。
Gunma to Niigata.

1068
00:38:48,636 --> 00:38:50,636
また難しそうな道。
Another rough-looking road.

1069
00:38:50,636 --> 00:38:53,636
あ、またこの道が途中で...
Ah, and this road also stops midway...

1070
00:38:53,636 --> 00:38:57,136
この辺は山ですし、絶対通れなさそう。
Around here is all mountains, there's no way you can drive through.

1071
00:38:56,136 --> 00:38:59,636
山。通れないのか。291号線。
Mountains. So it's impassable? Route 291.

1072
00:38:59,636 --> 00:39:01,136
ふんふん。
Mhm.

1073
00:39:01,136 --> 00:39:03,136
443。
Route 443.

1074
00:39:03,136 --> 00:39:04,636
うん、443。
Yeah, 443.

1075
00:39:04,636 --> 00:39:08,636
福岡から熊本。
Fukuoka to Kumamoto.

1076
00:39:08,636 --> 00:39:12,136
これも結構くっ、きっ...
This one is also quite cu-, sh-...

1077
00:39:12,136 --> 00:39:13,136
ぐるっと。
It loops around.

1078
00:39:13,136 --> 00:39:16,636
え、でも、比較的、比較的平野寄りかも、今までのな中だと。
Wait, but it might be relatively flat compared to the ones so far.

1079
00:39:16,136 --> 00:39:18,636
確かに。中だとね。
True, compared to the others.

1080
00:39:18,636 --> 00:39:21,636
割と市街地にたどり着い...
It reaches into fairly urban areas...

1081
00:39:21,136 --> 00:39:23,636
でも100、100km以上ありますね。
Still, it's over 100 kilometers long.

1082
00:39:23,636 --> 00:39:25,136
うん。遠い。
Yeah, that's far.

1083
00:39:25,136 --> 00:39:27,136
231。
Route 231.

1084
00:39:27,136 --> 00:39:28,836
231。北海道。
Route 231. Hokkaido.

1085
00:39:28,836 --> 00:39:33,136
札幌、北海道留萌。
Sapporo, Rumoi, Hokkaido.

1086
00:39:33,136 --> 00:39:36,636
どっちが、留萌市。どっちが札幌？
Which end is Rumoi City? Which is Sapporo?

1087
00:39:36,436 --> 00:39:38,136
こっち？
This way?

1088
00:39:38,136 --> 00:39:40,136
起点が...
The starting point is...

1089
00:39:39,636 --> 00:39:42,636
起点、こっちが札幌？ああ、なるほど。
The start... so this side is Sapporo? Ah, I see.

1090
00:39:42,636 --> 00:39:44,636
お、海沿いに行くんじゃない？
Ooh, doesn't it go along the coast?

1091
00:39:44,636 --> 00:39:50,636
そうだね。あ！あれ、ここ有名なあれじゃない？オロロンラインじゃないの？オロ、オロロンライン。
Right. Ah! Wait, isn't this that famous road? Isn't it the Ororon Line? The Oro- Ororon Line!

1092
00:39:50,136 --> 00:39:51,636
何それ？
What's that?

1093
00:39:51,636 --> 00:39:59,636
オロロンラインだ！あの、結構やはりこの、ドライブが好きな方には有名な、めちゃくちゃ景色がいいやつ。
It is the Ororon Line! It's super famous among scenic driving enthusiasts, with breathtaking views!

1094
00:39:59,636 --> 00:40:02,436
へー！やっぱ北海道の海って綺麗。
Ooh! The Hokkaido coast really is beautiful.

1095
00:40:02,436 --> 00:40:04,436
そうそうそう。オロロンラインきたー！
Yeah, yeah, yeah! The Ororon Line is here!

1096
00:40:04,436 --> 00:40:05,877
のじゃー！
Nojaaa!

1097
00:40:05,877 --> 00:40:06,477
...す
...is

1098
00:40:07,095 --> 00:40:11,197
ツーリングする方とかは、有名なのではないでしょうか。
It's probably quite famous among motorcyclists, wouldn't you say?

1099
00:40:08,677 --> 00:40:09,777
うーん
Yeah...

1100
00:40:11,277 --> 00:40:12,477
なるほど。
I see.

1101
00:40:11,977 --> 00:40:12,977
はい。
Yes.

1102
00:40:13,977 --> 00:40:16,427
そして、206。
And next, Route 206.

1103
00:40:17,627 --> 00:40:18,577
どこじゃ？
Where's this?

1104
00:40:18,977 --> 00:40:20,977
長崎！
Nagasaki!

1105
00:40:21,027 --> 00:40:22,177
ふんふんふん。
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

1106
00:40:22,727 --> 00:40:25,777
長崎も島が多いですけど...
Nagasaki has a lot of islands too, but...

1107
00:40:25,977 --> 00:40:30,577
長崎の中でも結構山々...ってか長崎全体的に山脈が...山が...
There are quite a lot of mountains in Nagasaki... or rather, Nagasaki has ranges... lots of mountains...

1108
00:40:30,727 --> 00:40:32,377
山が多い、坂が多い。
A lot of mountains, lots of hills.

1109
00:40:32,177 --> 00:40:33,577
山も坂も...
Mountains and hills both...

1110
00:40:33,177 --> 00:40:33,877
うん。
Yeah.

1111
00:40:34,027 --> 00:40:36,777
ここです。これでも地続きになってんだ、こう島...
Here it is. But this is actually connected by land, across islands...

1112
00:40:36,727 --> 00:40:37,827
え、すごい！
Whoa, amazing!

1113
00:40:37,677 --> 00:40:39,777
ね。海上区間ないから...
Right? There are no maritime sections...

1114
00:40:39,827 --> 00:40:40,877
じゃあ...
So...

1115
00:40:40,677 --> 00:40:43,177
めっちゃ、橋がかかって...それとも...
So lots of bridges are built... or maybe...

1116
00:40:42,477 --> 00:40:43,777
橋っぽいんじゃ、じゃあ。
So it's probably bridges, then.

1117
00:40:43,877 --> 00:40:44,977
ね。
Yeah.

1118
00:40:45,027 --> 00:40:46,727
長崎です。
That's Nagasaki.

1119
00:40:46,777 --> 00:40:48,077
ふむふむふむ。
I see, I see.

1120
00:40:48,177 --> 00:40:50,077
はい、114！
Alright, Route 114!

1121
00:40:49,577 --> 00:40:50,677
114。
114.

1122
00:40:51,177 --> 00:40:53,177
福島！
Fukushima!

1123
00:40:54,227 --> 00:40:55,877
これは短めかも？
This one might be on the shorter side?

1124
00:40:55,877 --> 00:40:57,477
ね、短めか。
Yeah, looks pretty short.

1125
00:40:57,577 --> 00:41:02,677
福島の、北の方の、東西ですね。
It runs east-west across the northern part of Fukushima.

1126
00:40:58,777 --> 00:40:59,877
ふんふん。
Uh-huh.

1127
00:41:02,677 --> 00:41:03,877
ふんふんふん。
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

1128
00:41:03,927 --> 00:41:05,677
114。
Route 114.

1129
00:41:06,177 --> 00:41:08,127
はい！レア！
Yes! A Rare!

1130
00:41:08,277 --> 00:41:09,527
短っくね？！
Isn't that super short?!

1131
00:41:09,377 --> 00:41:10,977
短っ！
So short!

1132
00:41:11,027 --> 00:41:12,077
なんだこれ？！
What is this?!

1133
00:41:12,127 --> 00:41:13,627
え、500メートル？！
Wait, 500 meters?!

1134
00:41:13,677 --> 00:41:15,177
足で走れる！
You could run that on foot!

1135
00:41:15,127 --> 00:41:16,377
走れる！
You totally could!

1136
00:41:16,477 --> 00:41:20,977
東京都港区から港区！
Tokyo, Minato Ward to Minato Ward!

1137
00:41:17,277 --> 00:41:18,177
うん、ほう。
Yeah, huh.

1138
00:41:19,077 --> 00:41:20,077
うん。
Yeah.

1139
00:41:21,077 --> 00:41:22,277
えっ？
Huh?

1140
00:41:22,877 --> 00:41:25,377
港区のどの辺じゃ？分かりづらっ。
Whereabouts in Minato Ward is it? So hard to tell!

1141
00:41:25,977 --> 00:41:28,377
あ、もう...短すぎて全然...
Ah, it's so short that it's not even...

1142
00:41:26,877 --> 00:41:31,677
あ、もう短すぎて...あの、示されてない、線が。
Ah, it's way too short to even be shown as a line on the map.

1143
00:41:31,877 --> 00:41:32,777
ね。
Right.

1144
00:41:32,877 --> 00:41:33,577
ほえー。
Whoa.

1145
00:41:33,627 --> 00:41:36,877
えー、500m来たよ、500m！レアです。
Whoa, 500 meters, we got a 500-meter route! It's a Rare.

1146
00:41:36,777 --> 00:41:38,577
130、短っ！
Route 130, so short!

1147
00:41:38,277 --> 00:41:39,577
短め。
Extremely short.

1148
00:41:39,627 --> 00:41:41,177
へえー。
Wow...

1149
00:41:41,277 --> 00:41:42,027
はい。
Yep.

1150
00:41:42,027 --> 00:41:43,777
こんな短いのがあるんじゃのう。
To think such short routes even exist.

1151
00:41:43,627 --> 00:41:44,577
ね。
Right?

1152
00:41:44,577 --> 00:41:46,677
長いイメージだったけど。
We had this image of them being really long.

1153
00:41:46,877 --> 00:41:49,577
こんな短いのあったら覚えられないな、わしゃ。
If they get this short, there's no way I could remember them.

1154
00:41:50,077 --> 00:41:51,777
よいしょ。次いくのじゃ。
Alright. On to the next one.

1155
00:41:51,727 --> 00:41:52,577
はい。
Okay.

1156
00:41:52,577 --> 00:41:55,877
はい。えー、322。
Here we go. Um, Route 322.

1157
00:41:56,377 --> 00:41:57,677
あ、これ出た？
Oh, did we get this one already?

1158
00:41:57,677 --> 00:41:59,477
え、待って、これ被った？
Wait, is this a duplicate?

1159
00:41:58,377 --> 00:42:01,077
出たかも！結構被るな。
We might have! We're getting quite a few dupes.

1160
00:42:00,677 --> 00:42:02,377
思ったより被る...
More dupes than I expected...

1161
00:42:01,177 --> 00:42:03,677
いや、思ったより被ってきたよ。
Yeah, we're getting way more dupes than I thought.

1162
00:42:02,677 --> 00:42:03,677
見たな。
Definitely seen this before.

1163
00:42:03,977 --> 00:42:04,877
次。
Next.

1164
00:42:04,877 --> 00:42:05,677
はい。
Okay.

1165
00:42:05,677 --> 00:42:07,977
44... あれ？これも...
Route 44... Wait, this one too...

1166
00:42:07,877 --> 00:42:09,077
これも見たか？
Did we see this one too?

1167
00:42:08,877 --> 00:42:10,077
これも見たか？
Did we see this one as well?

1168
00:42:10,127 --> 00:42:11,877
見たような予感が...
I feel like we have...

1169
00:42:11,477 --> 00:42:13,377
見たような予感ね、見たね。
That familiar feeling, yeah, we saw it.

1170
00:42:12,177 --> 00:42:14,377
福岡・熊本から...
From Fukuoka to Kumamoto...

1171
00:42:14,277 --> 00:42:16,377
だんだん被ってきました。
We're gradually getting more duplicates.

1172
00:42:16,177 --> 00:42:17,777
あ、これはまだか。
Ah, maybe this one's new?

1173
00:42:17,877 --> 00:42:19,777
こちら、289。
This one is Route 289.

1174
00:42:19,677 --> 00:42:23,677
お、新潟から福島。
Oh, Niigata to Fukushima.

1175
00:42:21,877 --> 00:42:22,877
いい。
Nice.

1176
00:42:24,677 --> 00:42:26,877
途中で切れてるね、これも。
This one is broken up in the middle too.

1177
00:42:26,877 --> 00:42:29,377
この辺もやっぱ山かな。
Must be mountains around here too.

1178
00:42:29,377 --> 00:42:30,777
はい、はい、はい、はい。
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

1179
00:42:30,777 --> 00:42:33,677
でも結構突っ切る、結構突っ切り...
But it cuts right through, really slicing across...

1180
00:42:33,677 --> 00:42:35,677
うわ、すごっ！
Whoa, amazing!

1181
00:42:34,877 --> 00:42:36,877
本当にもう分けている。
It truly splits it right in two.

1182
00:42:36,677 --> 00:42:39,277
本当だ！日本横断できるぜ。
It really does! You can cross right across Japan.

1183
00:42:39,277 --> 00:42:42,677
すごい。やっぱ横断できるの、なんか熱くなる、勝手に。
Amazing. Seeing a route cross all the way through just gets me hyped.

1184
00:42:42,577 --> 00:42:43,577
熱いね。
It is exciting.

1185
00:42:43,577 --> 00:42:46,677
ちょっと嬉しくなるのじゃ。潔い感じ。
It just makes me so happy. It feels so clean-cut.

1186
00:42:46,677 --> 00:42:48,377
潔い。
Clean-cut indeed.

1187
00:42:48,477 --> 00:42:49,577
次！
Next!

1188
00:42:49,577 --> 00:42:50,377
はい。
Okay.

1189
00:42:50,377 --> 00:42:51,877
えーっと、これ。
Um, this one.

1190
00:42:52,377 --> 00:42:53,877
16...

1191
00:42:53,277 --> 00:42:55,277
うわ、なんか変な形！
Whoa, what a weird shape!

1192
00:42:55,177 --> 00:42:56,877
奈良から...
From Nara...

1193
00:42:55,877 --> 00:42:57,877
奈良から和歌山...
From Nara to Wakayama...

1194
00:42:57,777 --> 00:43:01,677
あー！この山ん中突っ切ってくやつだ。
Ah! This is the one cutting right through the mountains.

1195
00:42:58,277 --> 00:42:59,477
奈良とか...
Nara and...

1196
00:43:01,677 --> 00:43:04,377
169と確か168で...
Route 169 and, I think, 168...

1197
00:43:04,577 --> 00:43:06,877
これって真っ直ぐなのは、あれ...
Is the reason it's so straight...

1198
00:43:06,877 --> 00:43:08,377
あー、確かに奈良...
Ah, true, Nara...

1199
00:43:07,677 --> 00:43:10,377
京都とか奈良...
Because it's Kyoto or Nara...

1200
00:43:08,877 --> 00:43:13,377
京都とか奈良だから、すごい...真っ直ぐなんかな。
Because it's Kyoto or Nara, maybe that's why it's so super straight.

1201
00:43:10,877 --> 00:43:14,377
区画が真っ直ぐ、昔から整備されてるから...
The city grid has been organized in straight lines since ancient times...

1202
00:43:14,177 --> 00:43:15,477
確かに、確かに。
Definitely, that makes sense.

1203
00:43:15,377 --> 00:43:17,677
でも和歌山らへんになって...
But once it gets around Wakayama...

1204
00:43:16,377 --> 00:43:18,477
シュシュシュシュッ...
It goes zig-zag-zag-zag...

1205
00:43:17,777 --> 00:43:18,877
そうそうそう。
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

1206
00:43:18,677 --> 00:43:20,477
これ山ですよ、これ。
These are mountains here, for sure.

1207
00:43:18,877 --> 00:43:23,177
峠道だから、山山山山ーって感じになってる。
Because it's mountain passes, it turns into pure mountain winding roads.

1208
00:43:23,077 --> 00:43:25,277
へー、カクカクしてんね。
Wow, lots of sharp twists and turns.

1209
00:43:24,877 --> 00:43:26,077
へー。
Huh.

1210
00:43:26,577 --> 00:43:29,377
あ、ここか、最長バス路線。
Ah, is this it? The longest local bus route.

1211
00:43:29,277 --> 00:43:33,377
へー。え、これも結構しっかり...ちょっとぼや...
Wow. And this one is quite clearly... wait, it's a bit blur...

1212
00:43:32,377 --> 00:43:33,577
ぼやけちゃう。
It gets blurry.

1213
00:43:33,477 --> 00:43:35,677
あー、これ山ん中ですわ。
Ah, yep, this is right through the mountains.

1214
00:43:35,177 --> 00:43:36,077
ね。
Right.

1215
00:43:36,177 --> 00:43:37,577
真っ直ぐと通って...
Running straight through...

1216
00:43:37,477 --> 00:43:38,277
ですね。
It sure is.

1217
00:43:38,677 --> 00:43:40,077
面白いのお、これ。
This is so interesting.

1218
00:43:40,077 --> 00:43:40,877
次。
Next.

1219
00:43:40,877 --> 00:43:41,777
次！
Next!

1220
00:43:41,877 --> 00:43:43,577
えーっと、こっちでもいいかな？
Um, can we go with this one?

1221
00:43:43,677 --> 00:43:46,277
347号。
Route 347.

1222
00:43:46,377 --> 00:43:48,077
お、山形！
Oh, Yamagata!

1223
00:43:48,077 --> 00:43:51,177
山形から、ちょっと見え...宮城。
From Yamagata to... I can barely see... Miyagi.

1224
00:43:50,677 --> 00:43:51,877
宮城。
Miyagi.

1225
00:43:52,377 --> 00:43:55,877
どっちが...どうなってる？後ろ見るのが遅い。
Which way does it... how does it go? I'm slow at checking the back.

1226
00:43:55,877 --> 00:43:57,377
なるほど。
I see.

1227
00:43:57,377 --> 00:43:58,877
ちょっとぼける。
It's blurring a bit.

1228
00:43:59,777 --> 00:44:03,277
え、クッカッて、クッてなってる。曲がってるのじゃ。
Wait, it's bent at an angle, like a notch. It takes a sharp turn!

1229
00:44:03,277 --> 00:44:05,777
これもあれか、山越え。
Is this one a mountain pass too?

1230
00:44:05,877 --> 00:44:07,177
ここも山。
Mountains here too.

1231
00:44:07,177 --> 00:44:08,377
山越えだ。
It's a mountain pass.

1232
00:44:08,677 --> 00:44:12,777
へー。でも山なのに結構真っ直ぐな道。
Huh. But even though it's in the mountains, it's a pretty straight road.

1233
00:44:12,877 --> 00:44:14,677
確かに、トンネル...
True, maybe tunnels...

1234
00:44:13,877 --> 00:44:15,477
そう、なんでじゃろう？
Yeah, I wonder why?

1235
00:44:15,377 --> 00:44:16,677
「へ」？
Like the hiragana "he"?

1236
00:44:16,377 --> 00:44:19,877
川の...川沿いだからかな？ここが。川沿い...なんでじゃろう？
Along a river... Maybe because it follows a river? Right here. Along a river... I wonder why?

1237
00:44:19,977 --> 00:44:23,277
そうだね、でもこれ多分県境は山だよね。
True, but the prefectural border is probably mountainous.

1238
00:44:23,177 --> 00:44:23,877
うん。
Yeah.

1239
00:44:23,877 --> 00:44:25,277
「へ」って形。
It's shaped like "へ".

1240
00:44:25,077 --> 00:44:27,277
「へ」って形。へー、面白い。
Shaped like "へ". Wow, that's interesting.

1241
00:44:27,677 --> 00:44:34,377
よし。なんか道のかたちで戦わせるバトルみたいなのやるなら、こいつ使いたい。
Alright. If we played some kind of battle game using road shapes, I'd want to use this one!

1242
00:44:34,377 --> 00:44:36,677
強そう！使えるかな。
Looks strong! Wonder if it would work.

1243
00:44:36,677 --> 00:44:41,177
なんかモジバケる？モジブレード？なんかそういうバトルに使うなら使いやすそう。
Like Mojibakeru? Or MojiBlade? It seems easy to wield in that kind of battle.

1244
00:44:41,277 --> 00:44:42,877
次行くのじゃ。
Let's go to the next one.

1245
00:44:42,777 --> 00:44:43,577
はい。
Okay.

1246
00:44:43,577 --> 00:44:45,377
えーっと、こちら。
Um, this one.

1247
00:44:45,877 --> 00:44:47,377
鹿児島！
Kagoshima!

1248
00:44:47,277 --> 00:44:48,577
鹿児島ー！
Kagoshima!

1249
00:44:48,577 --> 00:44:51,177
鹿児島をしっかりと突っ切っている。
It cuts right through Kagoshima.

1250
00:44:51,077 --> 00:44:52,177
本当だ。
It really does.

1251
00:44:51,877 --> 00:44:53,677
225号。
Route 225.

1252
00:44:53,677 --> 00:44:55,377
25... 225。
25... 225.

1253
00:44:55,677 --> 00:44:56,877
後ろ見るか。
Let's look at the back.

1254
00:44:57,377 --> 00:44:59,477
この辺... あ、こっちの方か！
Around here... Ah, over this way!

1255
00:44:59,477 --> 00:45:01,077
あー、こっちの方か。
Ah, it's on this side.

1256
00:45:01,265 --> 00:45:03,765
そうね。西側の鹿児島のほうね
Right. On the western side toward Kagoshima.

1257
00:45:02,265 --> 00:45:03,565
はいはいはい
Right, right, right.

1258
00:45:04,665 --> 00:45:06,165
え、じゃったら... ん？
Wait, if that's the case... Hmm?

1259
00:45:06,365 --> 00:45:08,165
桜島ってどこら辺にあるんじゃ？
Whereabouts is Sakurajima?

1260
00:45:07,665 --> 00:45:09,965
桜島真ん中に見えるんか
Can you see Sakurajima in the middle?

1261
00:45:09,765 --> 00:45:10,765
見えるかな？
I wonder if you can?

1262
00:45:10,965 --> 00:45:14,465
なんか先っちょのほうだと見えそう。こっち側からじゃと...
Near the tip it looks visible. From this side...

1263
00:45:13,965 --> 00:45:14,765
薩摩
Satsuma...

1264
00:45:15,065 --> 00:45:16,765
こっちに見えそうな予感
I have a feeling you can see it from this side.

1265
00:45:16,165 --> 00:45:19,065
ね。薩摩半島と大隅半島？
Yeah. Satsuma Peninsula and Osumi Peninsula?

1266
00:45:18,665 --> 00:45:20,265
ふんふんふんふん
Mhm, mhm.

1267
00:45:20,465 --> 00:45:21,865
枕崎
Makurazaki.

1268
00:45:21,765 --> 00:45:24,965
大隅って東？ こっちより東じゃっけ？
Is Osumi to the east? Was it east of here?

1269
00:45:25,265 --> 00:45:27,765
大隅のほうか。こっちが大隅？
Towards Osumi? Is this Osumi?

1270
00:45:26,765 --> 00:45:29,365
こっちが大隅？ こっちが薩摩じゃないかな
Is this Osumi? Isn't this Satsuma?

1271
00:45:29,165 --> 00:45:30,265
薩摩か
Satsuma, huh?

1272
00:45:30,265 --> 00:45:31,365
どっちじゃろ？
Which was it?

1273
00:45:31,165 --> 00:45:32,665
どっちでしたっけ？
Which one was it again?

1274
00:45:32,265 --> 00:45:34,465
わしもちょっとあやふやになってきた
My memory's getting a bit hazy too.

1275
00:45:33,665 --> 00:45:35,165
薩摩半島...
Satsuma Peninsula...

1276
00:45:34,965 --> 00:45:39,465
なんかこっちだったはず、大隅。違ったかな。こっち側だった気がする、わし
I thought Osumi was on this side... Was it? I feel like it was this side.

1277
00:45:39,465 --> 00:45:42,565
右が大隅、左が薩摩半島です
The right side is Osumi, and the left is Satsuma Peninsula.

1278
00:45:42,765 --> 00:45:44,265
よし。そして...
All right. Next...

1279
00:45:44,965 --> 00:45:46,565
えーっと...
Umm...

1280
00:45:48,365 --> 00:45:49,565
こちら！
Here it is!

1281
00:45:49,265 --> 00:45:50,165
はい！
Yes!

1282
00:45:50,965 --> 00:45:51,765
お！
Oh!

1283
00:45:51,065 --> 00:45:54,165
489！
489!

1284
00:45:54,565 --> 00:45:56,865
山口！
Yamaguchi!

1285
00:45:56,865 --> 00:46:00,265
山口県をしっかりと縦に行っている
It runs straight down vertically through Yamaguchi Prefecture.

1286
00:45:59,465 --> 00:46:00,165
うん
Yeah.

1287
00:46:01,365 --> 00:46:05,165
あ、山口県といってもだいぶ東のほうかも
Ah, though it's in Yamaguchi, it might be pretty far to the east.

1288
00:46:04,665 --> 00:46:05,865
本当だ
You're right.

1289
00:46:05,965 --> 00:46:07,865
だいぶ県の...
It's pretty much on the prefecture's...

1290
00:46:08,365 --> 00:46:09,765
ギリギリ...
Right on the edge...

1291
00:46:08,665 --> 00:46:10,265
ギリギリ...
Right on the edge...

1292
00:46:09,865 --> 00:46:11,465
ギリギリ山口じゃす
Barely inside Yamaguchi.

1293
00:46:10,865 --> 00:46:13,065
えー、島根に行かない感じか
Ah, so it avoids crossing into Shimane?

1294
00:46:12,565 --> 00:46:14,065
ぐらいな気がするのじゃ
It feels like that.

1295
00:46:14,265 --> 00:46:15,865
キラキラキラ〜
Sparkly sparkly sparkly~

1296
00:46:15,265 --> 00:46:16,265
これは...
This is...

1297
00:46:15,865 --> 00:46:17,165
短いのかな？
Is it short?

1298
00:46:17,365 --> 00:46:18,865
44km
44 kilometers.

1299
00:46:18,365 --> 00:46:19,665
44km
44 kilometers.

1300
00:46:19,165 --> 00:46:22,265
まあ、長すぎないぐらい。今の感じの基準じゃと
Well, not too long, by our current standards.

1301
00:46:21,665 --> 00:46:22,565
ね
Yeah.

1302
00:46:22,765 --> 00:46:23,765
えー
Huh...

1303
00:46:24,965 --> 00:46:28,965
あれ？ 50km以下がレアなんじゃったっけ？ なんかあったよね
Wait, wasn't under 50 km considered rare? There was something like that, right?

1304
00:46:28,865 --> 00:46:31,065
そうそうそうそうそう
Right, right, right, exactly.

1305
00:46:31,065 --> 00:46:32,665
なので短めなのじゃ
So it's on the shorter side.

1306
00:46:31,665 --> 00:46:34,465
短ければ短いほどレア
The shorter it is, the rarer.

1307
00:46:33,665 --> 00:46:34,865
短めなのじゃ
It's on the shorter side.

1308
00:46:34,465 --> 00:46:36,565
ここまでで何パックやった？
How many packs have we opened so far?

1309
00:46:36,265 --> 00:46:37,465
確かに
True.

1310
00:46:37,665 --> 00:46:40,665
意外と... 意外といっぱい用意したけど
Surprisingly... We prepared a lot, but...

1311
00:46:40,865 --> 00:46:42,165
1, 2, 3

1312
00:46:42,065 --> 00:46:42,765
4

1313
00:46:42,665 --> 00:46:44,865
4... 5! 5パック？
4... 5! Five packs?

1314
00:46:43,765 --> 00:46:45,465
5パックじゃ！
Five packs!

1315
00:46:45,465 --> 00:46:47,565
じゃあ2のほうもやるか
Let's move on to Pack 2, then.

1316
00:46:46,565 --> 00:46:48,265
確かに確かに！
Definitely, definitely!

1317
00:46:48,265 --> 00:46:52,165
2のほう... 意外と被りが出てきて
Pack 2... We've been getting quite a few duplicates...

1318
00:46:48,565 --> 00:46:50,465
意外と被りが出てきたのじゃ
Duplicates have been popping up surprisingly often.

1319
00:46:52,565 --> 00:46:56,165
じゃあ、今んとこSRが1枚ね
So we only have one Super Rare so far.

1320
00:46:55,565 --> 00:46:56,965
うんうんうん
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1321
00:46:56,965 --> 00:46:58,565
じゃあ2もやっていこう
All right, let's open Pack 2.

1322
00:46:58,365 --> 00:46:59,465
行くのじゃ！
Let's do it!

1323
00:46:58,965 --> 00:47:01,865
10パック用意したけど思ったより多かったわ
We prepared ten packs, but it turned out to be way more than I thought.

1324
00:47:02,065 --> 00:47:08,965
いや、てか、なんか、もっとサクサク見ちゃえば、結構すぐいっぱいSR見られるかと思ったけど
Well, I thought if we breezed through them quickly, we'd see a bunch of SRs right away, but...

1325
00:47:08,065 --> 00:47:10,365
いや、1つ1つ見たいからね
Well, we want to look at each one carefully!

1326
00:47:10,165 --> 00:47:14,465
そう！ 国道意外とおもろい！ わし全然、ミリ知らなんじゃけど
Exactly! National highways are surprisingly interesting! Even though I know practically zero about them.

1327
00:47:14,365 --> 00:47:16,465
2も見よう、みんな。2
Let's look at Pack 2, everyone! Pack 2.

1328
00:47:15,565 --> 00:47:17,365
気になっちゃうのじゃー
I just can't help being curious!

1329
00:47:16,765 --> 00:47:19,465
2、行くぞ、2。2
Pack 2, here we go, 2! 2!

1330
00:47:19,465 --> 00:47:20,665
国道2
National Highway 2.

1331
00:47:20,665 --> 00:47:23,065
では早速行きますのじゃ
Let's jump right into it, then!

1332
00:47:23,265 --> 00:47:24,465
こちら！
Here's this one!

1333
00:47:24,165 --> 00:47:25,065
はい！
Yes!

1334
00:47:25,065 --> 00:47:27,765
えー、192号！
Uh, Route 192!

1335
00:47:26,765 --> 00:47:27,665
お！
Oh!

1336
00:47:27,665 --> 00:47:29,365
すごい真っ直ぐ！
It's so straight!

1337
00:47:28,965 --> 00:47:30,865
真っ直ぐー！
Straight as an arrow!

1338
00:47:31,065 --> 00:47:35,265
地図的にはこっちかな？ 北がこっち側で...
Orienting the map, it's like this? North is this way...

1339
00:47:34,965 --> 00:47:36,565
192か
192, huh?

1340
00:47:36,665 --> 00:47:38,665
愛媛から徳島
From Ehime to Tokushima.

1341
00:47:38,265 --> 00:47:39,465
ほーう
Ooh.

1342
00:47:39,265 --> 00:47:40,365
なるほど？
I see.

1343
00:47:40,965 --> 00:47:43,365
すごいな。真っ直ぐ引いたな
Incredible. It's drawn completely straight.

1344
00:47:42,065 --> 00:47:44,965
日本地図で見ると、こっちで見ると...
Looking at it on the Japan map, from here...

1345
00:47:44,465 --> 00:47:47,265
おー！ すごい！
Whoa! Incredible!

1346
00:47:45,465 --> 00:47:47,965
すっごい真っ直ぐ行ってる
It runs amazingly straight.

1347
00:47:48,265 --> 00:47:50,465
これは何でこんな真っ直ぐ行けるんだ？
How can it possibly go so straight?

1348
00:47:49,565 --> 00:47:50,865
書いたように...
Like it was drawn...

1349
00:47:50,665 --> 00:47:51,765
あれかの？
Could it be that?

1350
00:47:51,265 --> 00:47:52,865
ペンで描いたように
Like it was drawn with a pen.

1351
00:47:52,765 --> 00:47:54,465
え？ これどうなってる？
Huh? What's the terrain like here?

1352
00:47:53,665 --> 00:47:54,665
真っ直ぐ
So straight.

1353
00:47:55,265 --> 00:47:58,265
ちょっと山とかも表記してくれるとすごい見やすい...
If they showed the mountains, it'd be so much easier to read...

1354
00:47:59,065 --> 00:48:01,465
え、どうなんだろ？ この辺り山脈...
Wait, I wonder? The mountain range around here...

1355
00:48:01,065 --> 00:48:04,165
うまく山を避けてる？
Did they skillfully avoid the mountains?

1356
00:48:03,765 --> 00:48:06,365
避けてるのかな？ 割と平地なのかな？
Did they avoid them? Or is it relatively flat terrain?

1357
00:48:06,265 --> 00:48:07,265
こんなとこ...
A place like this...

1358
00:48:07,365 --> 00:48:08,365
川沿いか
Along the river, maybe?

1359
00:48:08,165 --> 00:48:09,765
あ、川沿いか！
Ah, along the river!

1360
00:48:09,265 --> 00:48:10,365
はいはいはい
Right, right, right.

1361
00:48:10,165 --> 00:48:13,065
確かに川沿いなら行けるかも、こんな真っ直ぐさ
Indeed, if it follows a river, it could go this straight.

1362
00:48:12,165 --> 00:48:14,465
川に沿ってる感じするね、確かに
It definitely feels like it follows a river.

1363
00:48:13,965 --> 00:48:15,565
確かに確かに確かに！
True, true, true!

1364
00:48:14,965 --> 00:48:19,265
なんか国道からさ、その地形の構造みたいなのが見えてきますな
It feels like the national highways reveal the landscape's underlying topography.

1365
00:48:18,965 --> 00:48:22,165
ね！ 道ってそうかも。吉野川辺りか？
Yeah! Roads really do that. Around the Yoshino River?

1366
00:48:22,265 --> 00:48:27,265
うん。真っ直ぐ。なるほどなるほど。吉野川沿いね
Yeah. Straight. I see, I see. Along the Yoshino River, then.

1367
00:48:27,465 --> 00:48:31,665
次なのじゃ。こちら、220号！
Next up! Here, Route 220!

1368
00:48:31,465 --> 00:48:32,265
お！
Oh!

1369
00:48:32,265 --> 00:48:35,865
えーっと、九州かな？ 宮崎県から鹿児島
Umm, Kyushu? From Miyazaki to Kagoshima.

1370
00:48:35,065 --> 00:48:36,165
鹿児島
Kagoshima.

1371
00:48:36,165 --> 00:48:38,065
あ、それこそこっちが大隅のほう...
Ah, that's right towards Osumi...

1372
00:48:37,665 --> 00:48:39,265
お！ 大隅半島！
Oh! Osumi Peninsula!

1373
00:48:38,865 --> 00:48:43,765
あ、めっちゃ桜島に近くまで行ける道路だ！
Ah, it's a road that gets you super close to Sakurajima!

1374
00:48:39,765 --> 00:48:42,065
え、桜島近くまで行ける？
Wait, it gets that close to Sakurajima?

1375
00:48:43,765 --> 00:48:45,965
え、じゃあめっちゃ見えるんじゃない？ ここから
Then wouldn't you get an amazing view of it from here?

1376
00:48:45,465 --> 00:48:48,565
ねー。ちょっと見てみたいですね、桜島
Right? I'd really love to see Sakurajima.

1377
00:48:47,665 --> 00:48:50,465
海沿いを結構通った後に...
After following the coast for a while...

1378
00:48:49,565 --> 00:48:50,265
ね
Yeah.

1379
00:48:50,765 --> 00:48:54,465
100... でも187kmだからかなりあるね
100... But it's 187 km, so that's quite a distance.

1380
00:48:54,065 --> 00:48:55,865
なかなか遠目...
Quite a trek...

1381
00:48:55,765 --> 00:48:57,465
めっちゃカーブしてる
It curves like crazy.

1382
00:48:56,965 --> 00:48:59,965
ね。でも景色すっごい良さそう、ここら辺
Yeah. But the scenery around here must be amazing.

1383
00:48:59,565 --> 00:49:01,565
え、絶対いい！
Oh, definitely!

1384
00:49:02,265 --> 00:49:04,465
この桜島見たいよねー
I really want to see Sakurajima from here.

1385
00:49:04,365 --> 00:49:07,765
こんな感じなのだ、日本地図上見ると。よいしょ
This is what it looks like on the map of Japan. Here we go.

1386
00:49:08,065 --> 00:49:09,365
難しい...
This is tough...

1387
00:49:09,265 --> 00:49:10,365
ぼやける
It's blurry.

1388
00:49:10,365 --> 00:49:12,465
こうじゃない？ 微ボケ...
Isn't it like this? Slightly blurry...

1389
00:49:12,365 --> 00:49:14,465
微ボケYouTuber。なるほど
A slightly blurry YouTuber. I see.

1390
00:49:14,765 --> 00:49:17,465
そして次、あ、2桁なのじゃ！
And next—oh, it's a two-digit route!

1391
00:49:17,365 --> 00:49:18,565
こちら！
Here it is!

1392
00:49:18,365 --> 00:49:19,665
お！ 28
Oh! 28.

1393
00:49:19,765 --> 00:49:21,665
28号！
Route 28!

1394
00:49:21,765 --> 00:49:24,965
兵庫県から徳... え？！
From Hyogo Prefecture to Toku... Wait, what?!

1395
00:49:24,665 --> 00:49:26,365
あ、淡路島通ってる！
Ah, it goes through Awaji Island!

1396
00:49:25,965 --> 00:49:27,765
淡路島ー！
Awaji Island!

1397
00:49:27,965 --> 00:49:31,265
え、なんかすごい道の、道がいっぱいあるぞ
Wait, there are so many route lines here.

1398
00:49:31,065 --> 00:49:32,665
28なんだ
So that's 28.

1399
00:49:32,165 --> 00:49:35,465
ね、いっぱい分かれて、この淡路島の中でめっちゃ分裂して...
Yeah, it branches off a bunch, splitting up like crazy across Awaji Island...

1400
00:49:34,665 --> 00:49:36,565
なんで分裂してるけど...
Why is it split? But...

1401
00:49:36,065 --> 00:49:37,665
え、くねくねしてる！
Whoa, it's all wiggly!

1402
00:49:37,765 --> 00:49:43,765
これがじゃあ明石海峡大橋と鳴門大橋をこれ走る...
So this runs across the Akashi Kaikyo Bridge and the Onaruto Bridge...

1403
00:49:43,765 --> 00:49:44,965
橋の上の...
Across the bridges...

1404
00:49:43,865 --> 00:49:45,165
道やん！
It's that road!

1405
00:49:45,465 --> 00:49:47,565
へえ〜！
Whoa~!

1406
00:49:47,165 --> 00:49:48,965
淡路島横断！
Traversing Awaji Island!

1407
00:49:48,565 --> 00:49:51,565
じゃあもうほぼ淡路島のための道な気がする
So it's practically a road made just for Awaji Island.

1408
00:49:51,365 --> 00:49:53,265
確かに。他の県からね
True. Connecting it from other prefectures.

1409
00:49:52,765 --> 00:49:53,665
ね
Yeah.

1410
00:49:53,765 --> 00:49:55,165
いいですね
That's awesome.

1411
00:49:54,865 --> 00:49:56,965
こんな感じなのじゃ
Here's what it looks like.

1412
00:49:56,865 --> 00:49:59,265
すごい！ おおー！
Awesome! Whoa~!

1413
00:49:58,865 --> 00:50:00,565
もうこれは淡路島の...
This is practically Awaji Island's...

1414
00:49:59,965 --> 00:50:01,365
専用って感じ
Dedicated highway.

1415
00:50:01,265 --> 00:50:02,565
道路ですな
A dedicated road, indeed.

1416
00:50:02,906 --> 00:50:05,306
そして次がこちら！
And next up is this one!

1417
00:50:05,856 --> 00:50:08,656
345号
Route 345!

1418
00:50:07,156 --> 00:50:08,556
45号
Route 45!

1419
00:50:08,806 --> 00:50:11,456
新潟から... 山形
From Niigata... to Yamagata.

1420
00:50:09,006 --> 00:50:10,656
新潟から山形へと
From Niigata to Yamagata.

1421
00:50:12,056 --> 00:50:14,706
あ、もう本当にめちゃくちゃ日本海側...
Ah, it's really hugging the Sea of Japan coast...

1422
00:50:13,406 --> 00:50:15,656
あ、本当だ！日本海側を...
Ah, you're right! Along the Sea of Japan...

1423
00:50:15,756 --> 00:50:16,806
ここだけ。
Just right along here.

1424
00:50:16,806 --> 00:50:17,556
ね。
Yeah.

1425
00:50:17,856 --> 00:50:20,206
ん？新潟... こっちが山形？
Wait, Niigata... is this side Yamagata?

1426
00:50:20,556 --> 00:50:25,306
そうだね、山形から新潟... あ、いや、新潟から山形？
Right, from Yamagata to Niigata... Wait, no, from Niigata to Yamagata?

1427
00:50:25,906 --> 00:50:27,006
んー
Hmm...

1428
00:50:27,606 --> 00:50:33,806
でも、あんま... 山形ってそんなむちゃくちゃ他の東北の他の場所に比べて山は割と...
Though, not really... Compared to other places in Tohoku, Yamagata's mountains are relatively...

1429
00:50:33,906 --> 00:50:34,906
少ない？
Fewer?

